+# BN254 affine root/state correctness candidate
+
+This candidate replaces the residue root and all 33 ordinary state charts with
+six-word affine representatives. Its full equation/composition review is
+**pending**. Historical review labels, scores and rejection records for the
+monic programs do not qualify these changed programs. No official benchmark
+entry or score is updated by this source change.
+
+## Exact programs
+
+| Profile | VM model | Program | SHA-256 |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Native SI-MX3 | BCH-2026, three P2SH32 inputs | 8,108-byte imported code | `8e4cf7047756c426e1c36c33760d91a3890bede424abf45cf671017bbaa7aad6` |
+| Native SI-MX3 | same | 65-byte common redeem | `5551eff8d8f331a03be53af5aa6ce82328e82de44e5f789c3fe282138824509c` |
+| Rolled SI-GLS | proposed `bch-spec`, one P2SH32 input | 12,072-byte redeem | `33535d5dc0e3567960f89d27e6eacf098734333296146f9392f18836328ac4b7` |
+
+Native role IDs are 23, 24 and 25. Each native P2SH32 locking bytecode has
+SHA-256 `1f12637de917a090f23c7c9e59a916be1bf0fd4dfb52188d0e9fd415e0fa146d`;
+the rolled locking hash is
+`77fa297f4758733bcf29f053523a9eef3d95319e1cf6944ede3640567fd40d1d`.
+
+Ordered native code hosts are input0 C0 (4166 bytes, SHA-256
+`7f511033951f46339b0f280ed832728500344585c452bde971394b90b9d50b0a`) and input1 C1 (3942 bytes,
+`5ecb23bbe90e1afe876303c3ff33fe24aa84be7d0ee00321ed48efbf6a3f5367`). Their concatenation is the
+8,108-byte imported code above. The key-coordinate digest used by the native
+tag is `181aeefd9c0ce8d103ad084f4ef8174546852b0af46ac58a8061d4f38d346a6e`
+(SHA-256 of the20 canonical little-endian32-byte VK coordinates in protocol
+order). The default fixture/key file SHA-256 is
+`3d38e95a8f69a7c940b4ba03cc28c748254c07e5ff7957edb45665e45248cf91`.
+
+Pure reconstruction uses `buildProgram()` in
+[`bn-native-sound/script.mjs`](../bn-native-sound/script.mjs), or
+`buildRedeem()` in [`script.mjs`](script.mjs). Build parameters are default
+`SCHED_ITERS=4000`, `LAZY` disabled, balanced `CODE_SPLIT0`, and the default
+fixed-VK fixture file. Do not substitute another `BN_VK_FIXTURES` file under
+these hashes. The measured environment was Node26.12.0, noble curves2.2.0,
+and libauth3.1.0-next.8. Evaluation includes the benchmark's OP_DEFINE
+function-body accounting patch; an unpatched VM is a different cost model.
+
+## Equation and domain
+
+The key is the published BN254 key in
+[`public-fixtures.json`](../densless-recovered/public-fixtures.json), with
+exactly two public inputs. The intended accepted-run implication is
+
+```
+e(-A,B) * e(alpha,beta) * e(IC0+n0*IC1+n1*IC2,gamma) * e(C,delta) = 1.
+```
+
+A, B and C use finite affine encodings with canonical field coordinates;
+infinity encodings are unsupported. The source checks the G1 curve equations
+and the B twist equation. The B endpoint and checked inverse-norm trajectory
+are intended to enforce its prime-order subgroup. Public inputs are canonical
+`0 <= n0,n1 < r`. The folded pairing treats the public-input expression
+algebraically, including a neutral `vk_x` in the intended equation domain;
+no separate affine `vk_x` decoder is introduced. Complete compiled fold
+coverage remains part of the pending composition review.
+
+The claim concerns this fixed-key equation and domain. Arbitrary verifying
+keys, independent setup, circuit knowledge soundness, application zero
+knowledge, transaction authorization and live relay are separate claims.
+
+## Chart existence and serialization
+
+Let K=Fp12, E=Fp6 be its even subfield, sigma(X)=-X, and
+G=K*/E*. The new representative is
+
+```
+S_b(X) = 1 + b0*X + b1*X^3 + b2*X^5 + b3*X^7 + b4*X^9 + b5*X^11.
+```
+
+The six serialized words are b0..b5. They are never the first six
+coefficients of the expanded polynomial. Every encoded representative is a
+unit because its even component is 1. The chart covers G except [X]. Its
+quotient inverse is represented by sigma(S_b).
+
+Assume the standard BN field/order identities, valid nonzero raw class f,
+and a nontrivial reduced fixed-key pairing h whose quotient class has order
+r. There are r lambda-roots c0*h^i of f. Each recorded state has class
+H_j*c^(-k_j), with H_j independent of c and every NAF prefix k_j invertible
+modulo r. Each of 33 state charts excludes at most one root choice; the root
+chart excludes at most one more. Thus 35 distinct consecutive choices contain
+one usable choice for all 34 charts. The producer implements that bounded
+search. The multiplier h is a reduced pairing, not an unreduced Miller value.
+
+This proves chart availability under those hypotheses. The independently
+checked lattice decomposition also provides bounded 65-bit shifted scalar
+coefficients. Complete producer/VM liveness, including every other auxiliary
+encoding and resource condition, remains a separate obligation.
+
+## Arithmetic, ownership and transcript
+
+`EA` evaluates affine roots/states; `EV` retains the monic interpretation for
+fixed GT factors and Rconst. Both helper contracts and the affine Frobenius
+terminal recurrence have emitted-code checks. Every affine representative
+has degree at most11. The structural bound is `deg D <=311`, with at most
+150 odd quotient words; terminal `deg P+deg W <=64+22=86`.
+
+| Acceptance-dependent value | Intended owner/check |
+|---|---|
+| Point/scalar words | STMT/RD canonical decoders and curve predicates |
+| B slope and point update | BDBL/BADD inverse-norm zero equations |
+| B subgroup | full NAF trajectory and exact psi endpoint |
+| Delta slopes and fixed GT factors | fixed VK preprocessing and authenticated DS tables |
+| Root and 33 state records | WS or stream commitments before rho; computed transition identities |
+| Role handovers | canonical HENC/HDEC and predecessor byte equality |
+| Public-input fold | shared nibble bytes and exact integer relation modulo r |
+| Quotient | canonical words, structural cap, commitment before z and final Horner equality |
+| Imported native code | fixed framing, complete-code digest and common redeem/graph |
+
+The whole compiled owner/composition argument remains under review; this
+source map alone is not its proof.
+
+The new tags are `SIGLS/AFFINE1` and `BNMX3/AFFINE1 || VK_DIGEST`.
+The rolled h0 binds WS; native h0 binds DG, whose entries bind each owning
+stream and STMT. Then `rho_raw=SHA256(h0 || "rho")`. The final challenge
+binds h0, rho_raw and WQ (rolled), or the canonical input2 filler/WQ tail
+(native). Both challenges decode unsigned then reduce modulo p; z must be
+nonzero. A complete adaptive-oracle error budget for these exact programs
+must use the new degrees and the actual reduction distribution. It is not
+inherited from the old monic degree bound.
+
+## Existing-fixture evidence and remaining admission gates
+
+The two archives contain six distinct existing proofs: five source fixtures
+and five benchmark graphs overlap on fixtures0..3 only. The archived dense
+benchmark proof differs from source fixture4. Each original pairing
+equation passes a finite value-only group-MSM/four-pairing check. These six
+checks do not establish the pending universal compiled-equation implication. Their original
+proof/public-input prefixes remain exact; only dependent auxiliaries change.
+Both value references and both complete compiled profiles accept all six.
+
+Native evaluation uses local BCH-2026 standard and consensus models. These
+finite per-input/intra-transaction results do not establish live-chain or
+relay qualification. The largest
+observed unlocking is9,877bytes; minimum observed cost headroom is427,357.
+The measured primary score is28,793bytes and dense score29,369bytes, using
+the source's fixed6% padding policy and benchmark transaction accounting.
+These are local correctness-repair measurements. They are not optimization
+credit or official leaderboard results. Rolled acceptance uses proposed
+`bch-spec` modes and does not establish current-BCH admission.
+
+Final matrices contain36 native input verdicts and12 rolled-spec verdicts.
+Including standard padding probes gives72 actual input evaluations; the18
+final native standard verdicts are a subset of those probes. These are
+synthetic transaction contexts, not live transactions.
+
+Still pending: full exact-byte equation/owner/Fiat-Shamir composition;
+universal producer/resource completion; supplied rejection/full-harness
+qualification; and independent maintainer review. Named assumptions include
+field/tower and group identities, pairing correctness, fixed VK preprocessing,
+hash binding/random-oracle modeling and the declared VM semantics. Internal
+leaf proofs and positive fixtures do not supply blanket approval.
